messages:
jess: Heads-up from a quick handheld pass: when the sidebar is pinned on small widths the main table gets a horizontal scrollbar and rows clip. Screenshot in thread.
rory: I can repro on a Pixel 4a emulator. Our 420px breakpoint keeps the full sidebar too long; most phones sit under that.
quan: Two quick directions: icon-only vertical rail (persistent) or transient bottom sheet (on demand). Rail keeps one-hand reach for actions; sheet frees up horizontal space.
noor: For the rail, how wide would it be? 56px icon-only? Need to ensure 48x48 touch targets and persistent visible labels in a11y mode.
jess: Thinking thresholds:
- <=375px: transient bottom sheet from bottom (swipe to dismiss, full-width)
- 376-430px: compact rail (56px icons, long-press for labels)
- >430px: full sidebar
Agree?
rory: Sounds reasonable. A few UX nits:
- Add an affordance for the sheet opener (sticky bottom-right FAB) so users discover it
- Row-level actions should be reachable from the table row (ellipsis menu)
quan: For tables: prefer a single-line condensed row with ellipsized cells + a chevron to expand inline (accordion). Avoid navigating away to detail pages by default on mobile.
noor: Accessibility checklist:
- bottom sheet must trap focus while open and restore on close
- use aria-modal and role="dialog"
- mark the underlying content aria-hidden
- provide aria-live announcement when sheet opens/closes
- ensure icon-only buttons have accessible names (aria-label or visually-hidden text)
jess: Copy suggestion: change microcopy from 'Show details' -> 'Open details' and action menu item 'View' -> 'Open' on mobile for clarity.
rory: Implementation notes: long-press on icon should reveal a tooltip; fallback to persistent labels if reduced motion / a11y mode on.
quan: CSS sketch (very rough):
```
@media (max-width: 375px) {
  .sidebar { display: none; }
  .sheet { position: fixed; inset: auto 0 0 0; }
  .table .cell { white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
}
@media (min-width: 376px) and (max-width: 430px) {
  .sidebar { width: 56px; }
  .sidebar .label { display: none; }
  .sidebar .icon { width: 48px; height: 48px; }
}
```
noor: Also check focus order when toggling rail visibility; it should be predictable for keyboard/switch users.
jess: Action items: I'll draft a short spec with breakpoints and examples. rory, can you prototype the sheet opener and rail? quan can you do the inline expand prototype?
rory: Yep, I'll take the sheet + FAB and tooltip interactions. Planning a quick demo by Tue.
quan: I'll prototype the inline row expand and wire the copy change. Test plan includes VoiceOver and TalkBack.
a11y-bot: Reminder: add keyboard focus trap test, aria-live message test, and icon name verification. See internal doc: https://go/internal-a11y-mobile-patterns
jess: Thanks all 389 I'll create the ticket and link the prototypes.
